  "questions": [],
  "alt": "Recurring engineering work exposes a judgment and is handled by engineering the environment. The\n    environment supports the reasoner — models, knowledge, examples, procedures, context, skills, tools, evidence — and\n    enforces selected obligations — constraints, validators, permissions, gates, checks. A dashed arrow from\n    support to enforcement marks the recurring move of adding enforcement where feasible. The governed engineering\n    environment then hosts realization, enforcement mechanisms act on selected obligations, and work is realized. A\n    return edge runs from realized work back to recurring engineering work: its lower portion observes outcomes and\n    failures, and its upper portion improves the environment — the governance conversion of Section 3.4, where recurring\n    judgment can be encoded economically.",
